# Handoff and problems

## Duties (one job each)

Agents follow this table. [README.md](README.md) repeats a short pointer list for humans.

- `README.md` (git root) — Clone landing: two workspaces (`stardust/`, `stardust-ui/`).
- `stardust/outline.md` — Human intent (what/why). **Not executable.**
- `stardust/README.md` — Library: what it is / is not, layers, syntax (`.sd` / dumpable IR / Rust builder), `cargo test`.
- `stardust/waves.md` — **Live contract** (locks, parked gaps, named tests) plus **Archive (not executable)** of done **L1–L6 / I1–I7 / R1–R6 / O1–O8** full I/O/B. Do not start archived waves; they are `done`. No remaining coding-wave I/O/B.
- `stardust/assumption.md` — Confirmed = one-liners that **point** at `waves.md`; Unconfirmed = unanswered picks (including G1–G5). Not a third lock novel.
- `stardust/handoff.md` — Library resume stub (GNU linker, libffi, last wave).
- `stardust/kmod/stardust-kmdf/README.md` — Windows driver operator recipe.
- `stardust-ui/StarDust UI.md` — UI contract. Drive: `stardust-ui/desktop-drive.md`. Resume: `stardust-ui/handoff.md`.
- `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — Process only, not product.

Unanswered picks stay in `stardust/assumption.md` Unconfirmed and the [stardust/waves.md](stardust/waves.md) OOP lock. Open engineering gaps stay under Gaps parked in `stardust/waves.md`.

Do **not** create `specification.md` or a `docs/` tree unless Developer asks.

## ID namespaces

- Live remaining waves: **none.** Archive **L1–L6**, **I1–I7**, **R1–R6**, and **O1–O8** in the `stardust/waves.md` Archive section.
- Archive G1–G7 (in the `stardust/waves.md` Archive only): old aliases I5, I6, L3, L4, L5, R4, R5.
- OOP extras G1–G5 (private fields, static, abstract, `super`, StarDust bodies): unanswered in `stardust/assumption.md` Unconfirmed and the `stardust/waves.md` OOP lock (G1–G2 blank, G3/G4 later, G5 ask later).
- Integration tests: `stardust/tests/layout.rs`, `stardust/tests/import.rs`, `stardust/tests/region.rs`, plus feature-gated `python` / `llvm` / `haskell` / `linux_module` / `kmdf` / `attach`. Never O-wave ids. **Never name a test target, module, or function `index`.** Docs may say “matched sets” or “named tests,” not “index” as a code name.

## When to edit

- **Before code:** fill Review gates, accept/drop/reorder remaining waves, move a pick from `stardust/assumption.md` Unconfirmed into `stardust/waves.md` Locks.
- **After a named wave is `done`:** append that wave’s full I/O/B to the `stardust/waves.md` Archive section; add its named tests to the live matched-set list.
- Do **not** update docs as a substitute for executing a named wave.

## Read path

- **Human:** git-root `README.md` → `stardust/outline.md` → `stardust/waves.md` (locks + parked gaps + named tests). UI: `stardust-ui/StarDust UI.md`.
- **Agent executing a named wave:** that wave’s I/O/B in the `stardust/waves.md` Archive + Locks + that Review gate + the live named-test list. Open the Archive section when changing a done layer or chasing a named L/I/R/O test. There is currently no remaining coding wave.

## Hygiene (assumption / handoff)

Whenever you update `stardust/assumption.md` or a `handoff.md`:

1. **No datetimes.** Mark the newest finished task or newly added assumption with **`(Latest)`** (only one `(Latest)` per file section where it applies).
2. Fold durable outcomes into `stardust/waves.md` Locks or a short `handoff.md` gotcha.
3. **Delete outdated noise.** Prefer a short useful document over a complete diary.

Finished work in `handoff.md` needs no empty **Remaining** / **Notes**; omit those sections when nothing is left. Active work uses Done / Remaining / Notes.

## assumption.md

- **Two groups only:** `## Confirmed` and `## Unconfirmed`.
- **Confirmed:** one bullet per lock. Point at `stardust/waves.md` for detail. Do not reprint done-wave I/O/B.
- **Unconfirmed:** open choices Developer has not locked.
- When a lock is overturned, **delete** the old row and put the new rule in Confirmed.
